ABSTRACT

The E-Commerce Sales Analytics & Predictive Intelligence project is a complete data analytics and machine learning project developed using a large-scale e-commerce sales dataset containing 100,000 transaction records.

The project performs data preprocessing, feature engineering, Python-based data analysis, SQL business analysis, machine learning, predictive analytics, and interactive dashboard development.

Two machine learning models, Linear Regression and Random Forest, were implemented and evaluated using Mean Absolute Error (MAE), Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE), and R² Score.

An interactive Power BI dashboard was developed to display business KPIs, sales trends, category performance, customer behavior, top products, model comparison, actual versus predicted sales, and feature importance.

The project provides business insights and recommendations that can support inventory planning, product management, customer analysis, marketing planning, and data-driven decision-making.

1. INTRODUCTION

The growth of e-commerce has resulted in the generation of large amounts of sales and customer data. Analyzing this data helps businesses understand their performance, customer behavior, product demand, and sales trends.

The purpose of this project is to develop a complete analytics pipeline that converts raw e-commerce transaction data into meaningful business insights and predictive results.

The project combines:

Data preprocessing
Feature engineering
Python analytics
SQL analysis
Machine learning
Predictive analytics
Power BI visualization
Business intelligence

The project follows a complete workflow from raw data to business recommendations.

2. PROBLEM STATEMENT

E-commerce businesses generate large amounts of transactional data, but raw data alone does not provide meaningful business information.

There is a need for a system that can:

Analyze large-scale sales data.
Identify important sales trends.
Understand customer behavior.
Identify high-performing products and categories.
Perform business analysis using SQL.
Build predictive machine learning models.
Compare model performance.
Present results through an interactive dashboard.
Generate useful business recommendations.

This project addresses these requirements by developing an integrated analytics and predictive intelligence system.

