14. MACHINE LEARNING

Machine learning models were implemented for predictive analytics.

The following models were used:

14.1 Linear Regression

Linear Regression was implemented as a baseline predictive model.

It learns the relationship between input features and the target sales value.

14.2 Random Forest

Random Forest Regressor was implemented as an additional machine learning model.

Random Forest combines multiple decision trees to improve predictive performance.

15. MODEL TRAINING

The dataset was divided into training and testing data.

Training Data

Used to train the machine learning models.

Testing Data

Used to evaluate model performance on unseen data.

The trained models generate predicted sales values that can be compared with actual sales values.

16. MODEL EVALUATION

The models were evaluated using:

Mean Absolute Error (MAE)

MAE measures the average absolute difference between actual and predicted values.

Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE)

RMSE measures prediction error and gives greater importance to larger errors.

R² Score

R² Score indicates how well the model explains the variation in the target variable.

Model Comparison

