23. HOW TO RUN THE PROJECT
Step 1 – Install Required Libraries

Open the terminal in the project directory:

pip install -r requirements.txt
Step 2 – Load Data into SQLite
python SQL/load_data_to_sql.py
Step 3 – Run SQL Analysis
python SQL/run_sql_analysis.py
Step 4 – Run Machine Learning
python Model/predictive_model.py
Step 5 – Run Model Comparison
python Model/model_comparison.py
Step 6 – Generate Charts

Run the required chart-generation scripts from the Charts folder.

Step 7 – Prepare Dashboard Data
python Dashboard/dashboard_data.py
Step 8 – Open Power BI

Open Power BI Desktop and load the prepared data from:

Dashboard/Data/
Step 9 – View the Dashboard

Use the interactive Power BI dashboard to analyze the business KPIs, sales trends, customer behavior, product performance, and predictive results.

24. LIMITATIONS

The current project has some limitations:

The quality of predictions depends on the available dataset.
Sales behavior can be affected by factors not present in the dataset.
Customer behavior may change over time.
External factors such as market conditions, promotions, and economic conditions are not included.
Machine learning performance depends on feature quality and data distribution.
The current models may not capture all complex relationships in e-commerce sales data.
25. FUTURE ENHANCEMENTS

The project can be further improved by:

Using advanced time-series forecasting models.
Exploring seasonal sales patterns.
Adding more customer behavior features.
